1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,651
In working muscle, carbon dioxide and acid rise and the temperature goes up.

2
00:00:05,651 --> 00:00:09,375
All of these shift the curve to the right: the Bohr effect.

3
00:00:09,375 --> 00:00:15,546
At the same pressure, haemoglobin lets go of more oxygen exactly where it is needed most.

